  "prompt_text": "The figure is a simple schematic of an H-shaped waveguide or coupling structure. A broad blue pathway connects a lower horizontal section to an upper horizontal section through a central vertical channel labeled \\(W\\). An input field, marked \\(\\mathcal{H}^{\\mathrm{in}}\\), enters from below into the lower section, and an output field, \\(\\mathcal{H}^{\\mathrm{out}}\\), leaves upward from the top.\n\nInside the two side cavities formed by the H-shaped geometry are two yellow blocks, labeled \\(A_{a|x}\\) on the left and \\(B_{b|y}\\) on the right. Arrows point upward from the lower section into each block and then onward toward the upper section, indicating that energy or signal from the input region couples into both side elements and is transferred upward to the output region. The central vertical bar labeled \\(W\\) visually suggests a shared channel or interaction region linking the input and output while the side components participate in the transfer.\n\nOverall, the image conveys a symmetric two-branch coupling arrangement in which an incoming mode is split or mediated through two embedded elements before contributing to a single outgoing mode.",
